  "body": "Filed from TAG review of WebSocket in HTML spec: https://github.com/w3ctag/design-reviews/issues/268\r\n\r\n> Agree that retrofitting with Promises and Streams would be very helpful. @ylafon, @cynthia, @kenchris, @travisleithead and I support a ready Promise (as it doesn't appear sockets can be reopened). [...]\r\n\r\n> The reader and writer objects in the streams standard have a closed Promise which indicates when the stream is closed. I think this idea is almost directly applicable to the WebSocket API. Successful resolution means a clean close, rejection means some kind of error.\r\n\r\nWe would like to suggest that a `ready` and `closed` Promise-returning APIs be added to WebSockets, provided that there is implementer interest of course. :)\r\n\r\n@ricea",
